From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: abhay-byte <abhay02delhi@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 22:30:00 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] panvk: keep the depth flat for minDepth == maxDepth viewports
 biblioklept

Upstream widens a depth range below 37.7e-6 around its centre so the
window-space depth cull can still clip clip-space Z (dEQP
inverted_depth_ranges nodepthclamp_deltazero). For minDepth == maxDepth
that makes the written depth a +-1.9e-5 gradient instead of the exact
value the spec gives (z = minDepth). D3D MinZ == MaxZ viewports (sky
boxes, HUDs, depth-only passes at a fixed depth) rely on the exact value.

Only widen a non-zero range. A zero range now writes exact minDepth and
does not depth clip: its window Z carries no clip-space Z to cull on.
Cost: the 4 dEQP-VK.draw.*inverted_depth_ranges.nodepthclamp_deltazero
cases fail (out-of-range pixels are drawn at minDepth). They are not in
the prerast/sync/memory CTS gates.

Purpose: exact depth for DXVK MinZ == MaxZ viewports (PanProbe depth_stencil)
Tested GPU: Mali-G615 MC6 (Poco X6 Pro)
Tested Kbase UAPI: CSF 1.21 / MediaTek
Dependencies: csf-v11/076
Generated-by: LLM
---
diff --git a/src/panfrost/vulkan/panvk_cmd_draw.h b/src/panfrost/vulkan/panvk_cmd_draw.h
index eca1746..dc50e8b 100644
--- a/src/panfrost/vulkan/panvk_cmd_draw.h
+++ b/src/panfrost/vulkan/panvk_cmd_draw.h
@@ -342,7 +342,12 @@ panvk_viewport_z_coeffs(const struct vk_viewport_state *vp,
 
       if (dz < 0.0f)
          dz = -dz;
-      if (dz < PANVK_MIN_DEPTH_CLIP_RANGE) {
+      /* minDepth == maxDepth keeps the exact flat depth (D3D MinZ == MaxZ
+       * sky boxes and HUDs). Its window Z cannot cull clip-space Z, so such
+       * a viewport does not depth clip: inverted_depth_ranges deltazero
+       * draws its out-of-range pixels at minDepth.
+       */
+      if (dz > 0.0f && dz < PANVK_MIN_DEPTH_CLIP_RANGE) {
          float z_sign = z_min <= z_max ? 1.0f : -1.0f;
          float z_center = 0.5f * (z_max + z_min);
          float lo = 0.5f * PANVK_MIN_DEPTH_CLIP_RANGE;
-- 
